Okay, so this was my first ascension with a magic-using class.  Found
Gauntlets of Power in a store and wore them through the whole game
(actually, this isn't quite true; I found another pair on a wererat
later and wore that instead, giving my rusted pair to my pet vampire
lord.)  Anyway, used Magicbane and a stack of daggers where magic
failed, got a good amount of wishes, would've gotten a nice Staff of
Aesculapius if I hadn't already sacrificed for 5 artifacts.
Interestingly enough, I didn't find any (non-Minetown) altars at all
until level 8, which got me in a bit of a pickle, and then I found two
altars on level 8, an altar each on levels 9, 10 and 11, another altar
on 15 and a last one on 17.
I died once when a titan summoned nasties around me on Medusa's level.
After burning an amulet of life saving, I went back up in a hurry.
At one point I was stuck in Gehennom with no levitation item, and had
forgotten the spell, so I polypiled spellbooks for a while, out of
which I got a much-needed cone of cold spell.  Eventually I used the
Eye of Aethiopica to get back to my stash and refresh my magic.
I also sat around for a while with a succubus in the Wizard's Tower.
It was less obviously stupid than it might seem at first, because I was
standing in a doorway, monsters were coming nice and slow, and of
course it was no-teleport.  Unfortunately, like a butterbrain I
whistled my pet Olog-Hai in, and he smashy-smashed the succubus.  Oh
well.
I found a spellbook of magic mapping and I charmed some purple worms,
so Gehennom wasn't too bad.  On my way up I stopped at my stash to
refresh my spells and bring the spellbooks I would be needing the most.
At the second altar on Astral, I got the message "Vorpal Blade
decapitates the couatl!"  I immediately blasted the nearest player
monster with a finger of death and picked the Vorpal Blade up off his
corpse.  And, incidentally, said altar was the neutral one.

